--- hello.greet -- the canonical handl greeting.
---
--- Single source of truth for the `hello.greet(name)` logic.
--- `plugin-lib-stdlib` loads this file via `include_str!` (the `hello`
--- `ModuleSpec`), evaluates it to obtain the greet closure, and applies it
--- to the caller's argument. Handl's `+` operator natively concatenates
--- strings (`prim.add` / `bin_add`), so no module registry is required.
---
--- Contract: IsGreeting(output) -- output matches "Hello, <input>!"
cap "hello.greet"
name ~> "Hello, " + name + "!"
